VAR(H) FACTORIZATION:
  n=3: Var(H) = 3/4, numerator factors: [3]
  n=4: Var(H) = 3/1, numerator factors: [3]
  n=5: Var(H) = 285/16, numerator factors: [3, 5, 19]
  n=6: Var(H) = 585/4, numerator factors: [3, 3, 5, 13]
  n=7: Var(H) = 206325/128, numerator factors: [3, 3, 5, 5, 7, 131]


*** KEY PATTERN ***
The OCR denominator appears as the largest prime factor of Var(H) numerator!
  n=5: Var(H) = 285/16 = (3*5*19)/16,     OCR denom = 19 ✓
  n=6: Var(H) = 585/4 = (3^2*5*13)/4,       OCR denom = 13 ✓
  n=7: Var(H) = 206325/128 = (3^2*5^2*7*131)/128, OCR denom = 131 ✓

If this pattern holds, OCR(n) = 1 - k/(largest prime factor of Var(H)·2^m)
The denominator IS the largest prime factor of the numerator of Var(H).
